# ...but `host/wasm_worker_browser.js` is HAND-WRITTEN SOURCE, not output. It is
# the Web Worker script `host/web_browser.nim`'s `newBrowserWasmHost` starts by
# URL, and it lives beside that module because the two are one mechanism: the
# Nim side owns the protocol and the transport, this file is what runs on the
# other end of it. Without this exception the rule above -- which is about
# `nim js` artefacts -- would silently swallow a required runtime asset, and
# the bundle would ship without the only thing that can load a wasm module.
!src/frontend/viewmodel/host/wasm_worker_browser.js
# ...and so are PLAT-18's slice host files. They are the HOST HALF of the
# vertical slice — the frame applier, the schedule, the emscripten bridge and
# the Electron main process — hand-written JavaScript that
# `ci/test/plat18-electron-slice.sh` copies beside the three compiled arms.
# Without this exception the `nim js` output rule above swallows all four, and
# the script is committed pointing at files nobody else has: a harness that
# runs only on the machine it was written on, which is the shape §14c of
# Verification-Harness-Traps.md is about one level down. Found by
# `git add -N` before the pre-commit measurement (§16d), which is the whole
# reason that step exists.
!src/frontend/viewmodel/tests/manual/plat18_slice_host/*.js
